      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report a case of coronary artery bypass grafting using left intra thoracic artery (LITA) in a 63-year-old male with Buerger's disease. His coronary angiography showed a long lesion seemed rosary in the left anterior descending (LAD). At operation, the surface of the coronary artery was dark red with white speckles. The LAD was opened distal end of disease, the intima of the coronary artery made much soft thin fold. The disease was never atheromatous. His coronary angiography showed a very rarely finding that seemed rosary."},
